WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.529
Eight identical copies of the King James Bible
were selected for experimentation.

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:07.289
The first copy was placed in the machine on
the setting “Coarse.”

00:00:07.289 --> 00:00:11.650
The output produced was one sheet of leather,
a small block of wood, a stack of rags stained

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.500
with ink, and a reel of thread.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.090
“1:1” produced one copy of the Qur’an.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.860
On “Fine” the output was a book with lead
pages and a golden cover, written in an unidentified

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:21.860
language.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.989
On “1:1” it produced a copy of “The
Satanic Bible.”

00:00:24.989 --> 00:00:29.429
On “Very Fine” the output was a book with
seemingly infinite pages, currently at a page

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:34.850
count of two million, encompassing religious
texts from all known faiths in all known languages,

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.160
as well as some religions that have previously
never been seen before.

